129 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 95 0 R
/E (Traffic congestion is a common problem in urban areas that causes travel delays, increased fuel consumption, and inconvenience to commuters. This project focuses on predicting traffic congestion levels using Machine Learning techniques. Historical traffic data containing factors such as vehicle count, average speed, traffic density, weather conditions, and time of day is analyzed and preprocessed. Two machine learning algorithms, Random Forest and Gradient-Boosted Trees, are implemented to classify traffic congestion into different levels such as Low, Medium, and High. The performance of both models is evaluated using suitable metrics such as accuracy, precision, recall, and F1-score. The models are then compared to identify the better-performing approach. The proposed system can help understand traffic patterns and support better traffic management and planning.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
